ff legitimately; never silently recreate the signature. [Task 1][Task 4]\n- The ledger state machine is `PENDING` through `NEEDS_USER` and `PASSED`/`LOCKED`; a second hard failure after one content repair becomes `NEEDS_USER`. `accept-user-exception-candidate` is deliberately narrow: accept only a `NEEDS_USER` current candidate whose SHA matches the Frame Contract/Visual profile, record the user approval text and `direct_user_review_exception_acceptance`, then set `PASSED`. Do not hand-edit JSON to bypass the gate. [Task 2]\n- `visual_lock_v21.bind-from-queue` must bind all required images. A `scout_repair` candidate is eligible only when the ledger is PASSED, lineage SHA matches the current candidate, and the direct-acceptance audit matches. `INPUT_IMAGES_UNAVAILABLE` is evidence absence, not content failure; preserve it and use `restore-evidence-gap-review` only for the defined mis-downgrade case. [Task 2][Task 3]\n- Visual Lock V2.1 accepts policy exactly `four_admission_v21`; `four_admission_v21_1_plus_3` is not recognized. The four roles are ordinary baseline → worst capture condition → first major anomaly → high-impact admission; this episode bound 01/05/08/17, but `validate_episode.py`/`machine_gate.py`/`evidence_gate.py` remain the sole legal progression gates. [Task 2]\n- Windows critic shield: pass Chinese prompt text as UTF-8 bytes rather than `text=True`; copy Chinese-path images to ASCII temporary attachments before `-i`; clean up the temporary directory. `CreateProcessWithLogonW failed: 1385` means the worker cannot inspect pixels, so record `INPUT_IMAGES_UNAVAILABLE` and do not claim Visual Lock pass. [Task 3]\n- Progress reports belong in `episodes/<episode>/meta/`, not frozen `story/`. Separate machine-stage, candidate-frame, PASSED-frame, approved-frame, and weighted-work-package percentages rather than calling generated files completed production. [Task 4]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Symptom: `visual_lock_v21.py show-plan` says V