efore closing a receiver for offline assertions because MQ delivery can still be in flight. [Task 1]\n- Both forward and rollback scripts start with `USE DB_YOPU_IM;`. The forward migration covers mention tables and the listed session/offline/pending columns; rollback uses INFORMATION_SCHEMA guards and `DROP ... IF EXISTS`, deletes structure rather than backing up data, and therefore requires the feature off plus a data backup before execution. [Task 2]\n- Current dev failure signature: group send cmd=12 returns `2006010` when V2_ONLY reads a group whose policy and member manifests have divergent versions. Check group policy/recipients/member manifests in Redis plus `DB_YOPU_CRM.TB_IM_SNAPSHOT_DOMAIN_VERSION`; this was reproduced on a non-test group, so it is not a test-account exception. [Task 3]\n- The current reader strictly requires `policy.version == member.version`, while domain-local writes can increment member/recipients without policy; mismatch is only metered, and reconcile repairs missing rather than version-divergent domains. Do not hand-edit code/data during diagnosis; choose and review either a coherent group-level version model or synchronized write-side versioning. [Task 3]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Symptom: sms-login test reports an ID mismatch or crashes writing emoji. Cause: userId is a string and Windows console is GBK. Fix: normalize once with `int(...)` and configure UTF-8 replacement output. [Task 1]\n- Symptom: offline test wrongly treats an in-flight group push as a defect. Cause: a different MQ instance may consume then route back after the client closes. Fix: add a delivery wait before close and use server log timing to classify the race. [Task 1]\n- Symptom: `apply_patch` says `multiple operations target ...`. Fix: do Delete and Add for the same file in separate patches. [Task 1]\n- Symptom: any ordinary group send fails `2006010` before @ validation. Cause: V2 authorization cross-domain version mismatch under Mode C f