E, CALL_DEBUG, getUserRoutes, route:user:clients, SIGNAL_EXCHANGE, consumeSignal, 音视频信令投递失败，用户不在线, AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE, b001ea6ac\n\n## User preferences\n\n- for an IM symptom report, the user twice replied only “继续” during investigation -> continue the read-only chain (memory → code → git history → executable evidence plan) rather than stopping early for speculation or unnecessary clarification. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Call chain is `IMHandler.handleCallInvite` → `IMServiceImpl.initiateCall` → `CallServiceImpl.initiateCall` → `sendCallSignal(calleeId, CALL_INVITE)`. It is synchronous on the Netty worker and does not pass `authorizeSingleChat` / `RelationAuthorizationSnapshotReader`; `AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE`, friend-snapshot fence, and welcome-message conclusions do not explain call delivery. [Task 1]\n- `sendCallSignal` chooses local `channelManager.sendToUser`, remote `MessageProducer.sendSignal` to `SIGNAL_EXCHANGE` with `{serverId}.signal`, then direct fallback when `hasActiveChannel`. `MessageConsumer.consumeSignal` ACK-drops a remote signal if the callee has no active channel: “信令无重试队列/DLQ，直接丢弃并告警.” [Task 1]\n- Route model is per-client `yopu:im:route:user:{userId}:{clientType}` plus client set `yopu:im:route:user:clients:{userId}` and legacy single key; online means `onlineStatus==1`, TTL 180s. On this checkout `CALL_DEBUG=true`; inspect `routeCount`, decision/fallback lines, the offline warning, and client CALL_INVITE/UI evidence before ranking root causes. `routeCount=0` while online points first to a missing clients-set write. [Task 1]\n- Historical route leads: `b001ea6ac` covers non-atomic RBatch route writes/client-set loss; `86de7f055` covers RBatch read contention via getAsync+30s cache. The candidate retry/refresh/client UI remedies remain proposals until runtime evidence selects one. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Do not analogize call behavior from single-chat authorization snapshots before tracing the actual call path; the initial AUTH_SNAPSHOT hypothesis was disproved. [Task 1]\n- In PowerShell, `find` can return `Parameter format not correct` and formatted `Select-Object FullName` can truncate paths. Use `Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Filter 'Name.java' | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName }` or an exact full path. Probe dev endpoints with bounded parallel short timeouts after confirming connectivity. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: dashi-taskboard (Codex Taskboard) evaluation, local install, and Windows integration\nscope: Evaluate, install, and diagnose the local Codex Taskboard; distinguish its own task database from existing Codex tasks and keep the Windows service loopback-only.\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=repository stars, release activity, package versions, defaults, and CI state are time-sensitive; the evaluation workflow and local-network security checks are reusable.\n\n## Task 1: Evaluate and locally install chuspeeism/dashi-taskboard\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n\n### keywords\n\n- dashi-taskboard, chuspeeism/dashi-taskboard, Codex Taskboard, React 19, Node 22, SQLite, Tauri, taskctl, npm ci, npm run check, /health, CODEX_TASKBOARD_HOST, 0.0.0.0:47823, 127.0.0.1, CDP, CSP, Windows unsigned\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user writes “dashi-taskboard 看看这个github仓库” without criteria -> respond in Chinese and proactively use a structured repository assessment (identify → README/metadata/direct files → maturity/activity/risk → actionable trial recommendation), not a one-paragraph summary. [Task 1]\n- when the user says “看不到我codex正在执行的任务啊” -> explain that the browser version tracks only tasks created in its own database; it does not import existing Codex tasks, and tracking starts from Taskboard. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Prefer the direct GitHub repository page and raw `README`/`package.json`/`AGENTS.md`/`LICENSE`/`PRIVACY.md` plus CI and commits over stale search snippets; search-result star counts diverged during this review. [Task 1]\n- The captured project was a local-first React 19 + Node 22 + SQLite + Tauri taskboard with `taskctl` and an internal Codex Skill using the same HTTP API. Default host `0.0.0.0:47823` has no LAN account authentication; for a local trial explicitly set `$env:CODEX_TASKBOARD_HOST = '127.0.0.1'`. Install at `D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\dashi-taskboard` with `npm ci` then `npm run check`; verified health endpoint is `/health`, not `/api/health`. [Task 1]\n- The independent browser service cannot scan/import arbitrary existing Codex chats. For tracked work use Taskboard create task → “open in conversation” → Codex processes it → `taskctl` records `CODEX_THREAD_ID`. [Task 1]\n- On Windows/MS Store Codex, the source Launcher failed `Unable to inspect the launched Codex process`; prefer the official NSIS installer if the user explicitly confirms its unsigned installer. Verify a resumed download's SHA-256 before opening it. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Symptom: search results disagree on repository statistics. Fix: cite/decide from the current direct repository page and raw files, not cached search cards. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: Windows Codex C-drive cleanup, image junction, and build-ios-apps memory-pressure diagnosis\nscope: Free C-drive capacity safely, preserve the D-drive image junction, and diagnose Codex-plugin process leaks that exhaust commit memory and crash IDEA.\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=the machine paths, sizes, and free-space figures are local snapshots; the C-drive triage order, D-drive image junction, and deletion safeguards are reusable on this machine.\n\n## Task 1: C盘满 – inspect first, remove archived sessions, and move generated images to D:\\codex-img\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-15T08-36-48-OgLK-c_drive_cleanup_codex_junction_img_migration_idea_memory_cra.md (cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex