t_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\26\\rollout-2026-08-26T11-29-01-01a022ec-756e-7550-8c81-f92d7843c126_01a03c1d-30d1-7be3-979a-0958cee40032.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T05:39:09+00:00, thread_id=01a022ec-756e-7550-8c81-f92d7843c126, success: staged compatibility explanation; the proposed checklist was not separately adopted)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Phase 0-5, dual-write, SHADOW, domain-read, legacy-write, AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE, COMPLETED, PENDING, RETRYING, FAILED, manifest READY, mismatch, REPAIR Outbox\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user asked “给我一个新的 md” -> Redis/IM analysis documents in this repo should use the existing `主题-YYYYMMDD` naming and `docs/architecture/` placement. [Task 1]\n- when the user asked “每一步实施完都能兼容旧的缓存吗” -> state the mechanism and the “断旧” boundary per phase, not a blanket “能”. [Task 3]\n- when the user asked “什么时候需要检查下是否双写全部成功，同时对齐” -> provide a “何时/查什么/通过标准” cutover checklist. [Task 3]\n- when the user says “dev部署了，重新测试” -> first verify the deployed JAR/process is the intended fix, wait for RETRYING Outbox convergence, then run the complete acceptance chain rather than only rerunning assertions. [Task 2]\n- when the user asks “评审，如果不通过则补强继续评审” -> use a formal blocking-item loop and state a clear pass/fail outcome; do not leave unresolved correctness or privacy gaps under a nominally reviewable contract. [Task 3]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- One Redis key must use one codec: use `StringCodec` for authorization/profile snapshots, private views, fence/ready, and Lua state; the `RedisConfig` default `JsonJacksonCodec` is for DTO/Map/object caches. The historical `yopu:im:ack:pending` single/batch/retry mix caused `InvalidTypeIdException: missing type id property '@class'` and was unified on 2026-08-25. [Task 1]\n- Phase 0-5 cover 11 of 14 snapshot domains; `GROUP_STATS`, `FRIEND_VIEW`, and `GROUP_MEMBER_VIEW` remain unplanned. JetCache's Java `value-encoder` is a separate modernization line, and `deliver:*` serialization must be confirmed by environment scan because its declared `RedisTemplate<String,String>` conflicts with the injected Jackson-valued bean. [Task 1]\n- The Phase 3 11-step dev test validates formal+manifest version rows, fences, Outbox `COMPLETED`, and legacy group writes across create→join→admin→member mute→mute-all→review→kick→leave→dissolve. V2 keys use real `{gid}` hash tags; legacy `yopu:im:auth:group:%d:snapshot` has no braces. [Task 2]\n- Script sequencing matters: capture Outbox baselines before `createGroup`; enable `allowMemberMute` before member mute and do it before mute-all; review-list members must be normal, roleType=0, and unmuted. `member:index` materialization is P3-C2 and is expected to be absent in P3-A4~A7. [Task 2]\n- Phase 4 v0.3 covers PROFILE_SUMMARY/FULL/STATS, GROUP_PROFILE/STATS, FRIEND_VIEW, and GROUP_MEMBER_VIEW. Private view uses field-level complete envelopes and Lua CAS rather than an owner manifest; new `*_V2` Outbox relation types isolate rolling releases; JSON/field envelopes use `SHA256_CANONICAL_JSON_V1`, while Set domains retain `SUM128_V1`. [Task 3]\n- Safety fences are mandatory for privacy/history-sensitive changes: set before DB fact changes; a failure to acquire must block commit; fences clear only via the matching higher-version commit or mutationId-scoped REPAIR. `ConversationServiceImpl#resolveGroupJoinTimeEpoch` must fail closed when joinTime is unavailable, not skip history filtering. All readers/processors must recognize fences and `*_V2` types before writers are enabled. [Task 3]\n- Phase 0-4 retain compatibility through old+new writes, SHADOW dual-read, and default-false domain-read switches; Phase 5 is the “断旧” point. A dev pass does not waive Cluster same-slot proof, seven-day SHADOW zero difference, fail-closed/rollback drills, reconciliation tamper test, DBA version-row capacity, or P1 performance gates. [Task 4][Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- A post-create Outbox baseline causes false timeout because the create transaction has already inserted records; sample first. Do not put braces in legacy-key checks, and SKIP unimplemented P3-C2 member-index assertions. [Task 2]\n- A contract with an unproven atomic algorithm, reused Outbox type that old processors can prematurely complete, weak JSON checksum, or privacy-expanding default is not ready to pass static review. Close those blockers before declaring pass. [Task 3]\n- `apply_patch` Add File needs a blank `+` line immediately after the header or it can fail with `invalid hunk ... is not a valid hunk header`. In PowerShell, use `rg 'pattern' docs/architecture -g '*.md'`, not `docs/architecture/*.md` (os error 123). [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM conversation-list 500 from conv:last cache corruption\nscope: Diagnose a missing friend-approval message when a participant's IM conversation list fails; use for Redisson `HGETALL` decode errors, `conv:last` anomalies, and cache-first remediation design.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=affected users, keys, logs, dev host, and branch `sprint3-0826-147` are time-specific; the per-user list verification, bad-key scan, and three-layer fix are reusable.\n\n## Task 1: Separate welcome-message delivery from the conversation-list 500 and locate corrupt conv:last keys\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T05-44-53-a2qD-im_convlast_cache_corruption_list500_friend_approval_welcome.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-20T13-44-53-01a01db3-6d5a-70a2-ac77-3c4429898d1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-21T09:18:02+00:00, thread_id=01a01db3-6d5a-70a2-ac77-3c4429898d1b, partial: cache deletion and self-heal verified; durable read/write hardening documented, not implemented)\n\n### keywords\n\n- 好友申请通过, 消息列表不显示, 会话列表500, conv:last, ConversationServiceImpl, getRecentConversationList, readAllMap, HGETALL, CommandDecoder, JsonJacksonCodec, InvalidTypeIdException, RBatch, batchCacheLastMessage, applyLastMessageFallback, hlen!=3\n\n## Task 2: Produce the three-layer production investigation and repair plan\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T05-44-53-a2qD-im_convlast_cache_corruption_list500_friend_approval_welcome.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-20T13-44-53-01a01db3-6d5a-70a2-ac77-3c4429898d1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-21T09:18:02+00:00, thread_id=01a01db3-6d5a-70a2-ac77-3c4429898d1b, success: production investigation and repair runbook delivered; per-environment scan and approval still required)\n\n### keywords\n\n- IM-会话列表500-会话最后消息缓存损坏-修复方案.md, hlen=3, readAllMap try/catch, applyLastMessageFallback, Redis SCAN, RBatch 并发异步命令, 87c737e1e, 86f848291, X-User-Id\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when defining the message behavior, the user corrected “方向错了，是A加B，B同意后，给A发消息：你好，我是B ... 且A消息列表1条未读” -> do not invent bilateral system messages; preserve the requested B→A direction and receiver-side unread semantics. [Task 1]\n- when the user says “大白话介绍给我” / “大白话解释” -> explain the causal chain with a plain-language analogy before the technical details. [Task 1][Task 2]\n- when the user asks “生产也存在这个问题啊，我怎么排查” -> give a step-by-step, executable production runbook: reproduce with user identity, inspect HGETALL/CommandDecoder logs, scan all keys, identify affected users, stop the bleeding, then deploy the durable fix. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- First validate each participant independently. In this incident, the B→A welcome message was already persisted and A's list worked; B's list returned a business 500 because an unrelated old group `conv:last` cache entry failed to decode. Do not equate a missing UI item with a failed message-generation chain. [Task 1]\n- `ConversationServiceImpl.getRecentConversationList` calls `redissonClient.getMap(key).readAllMap()` inside a stream without per-conversation protection. A decode exception from one `conv:last` key bubbles through `GlobalExceptionHandler`, so one bad cache entry takes down the complete list even though `applyLastMessageFallback` can rebuild a normal cache miss from `TB_MESSAGE`. [Task 1]\n- Expected key is `yopu:im:conv:last:{userId}:{sessionId}:{scope}` (`scope` 0 public, 1 private) with exactly three quoted hash fields: `\"msgType\"`, `\"content\"`, `\"sendTime\"`. A practical non-mutating detector is a Redis `SCAN` over `yopu:im:conv:last:*` and `HLEN`; investigate `hlen!=3`, especially ETX-prefixed/UTF-8-truncated field names. Never carry a development scan result into production: rescan each environment. [Task 1][Task 2]\n- Deleting a confirmed corrupt `conv:last` key is cache-only stop-the-bleeding: the next read invokes `applyLastMessageFallback`, reads the last message from DB, and repopulates the normal 30-day TTL cache. Verified in dev, but production deletion requires a freshly verified key list and authorization. [Task 1]\n- Durable repair has three layers: A delete confirmed bad cache keys; B wrap `readAllMap` with per-key `try/catch`, warn with user/session/key, evict and fall back to DB; C replace the remaining `ConversationServiceImpl.batchCacheLastMessage` two-step RBatch write path with concurrent async commands, consistent with the related `87c737e1e` repair. The RBatch issue is strongly suspected, not fully proven as the unique writer root cause. [Task 2]\n- The user's earlier account-side `86f848291` welcome-message reliability change is not the cause: it makes B→A delivery reliably triggered/idempotent; it does not repair a corrupt list-preview cache. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Symptom: one party sees the conversation and the other does not. Initial mistake: attribute it to missing “通过” message generation or propose bilateral welcome messages. Fix: call both users' list endpoints and inspect business status before changing delivery logic; then follow message DB, session index, and list/cache data separately. [Task 1]\n- Symptom: a request looks successful at HTTP level but client behavior is a list failure. Cause: the API can carry business `code=500` even when transport is HTTP 200. Fix: inspect the application response body and server logs, not HTTP status alone. [Task 1]\n- A large `apply_patch` document failed with `is not a valid hunk header` because an added line lacked `+`. For a large MD repair plan, ensure every new line in an added hunk has the prefix or split the document into smaller, checkable patches. [Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / yopu-im-core message-collection USED_BYTES quota repair and test backfill\nscope: Repair media collection quota accounting when displayed used space stays at 0B, and safely backfill the test database after contract-aligned code validation.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=server addresses, branch, target user, and current schema are environment-specific; the physicalBytes settlement, atomic quota, and backfill verification rules are reusable.\n\n## Task 1: Repair final physical-byte settlement and permanent media rejection\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T11-18-11-HAhd-yopu_im_message_collection_used_bytes_quota_fix_and_backfill.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-2026-08-20T19-18-11-01a01ee4-93b1-7932-873a-261aceb63f03.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T11:36:39+00:00, thread_id=01a01ee4-93b1-7932-873a-261aceb63f03, success: focused tests and package passed)\n\n### keywords\n\n- 消息收藏, 已用空间, USED_BYTES, RESERVED_BYTES, convertReservedToUsed, physicalBytes, settlePhysical, completeMediaTask, FILE_TOO_LARGE, QUOTA_BYTES_EXCEEDED\n\n## Task 2: Execute and verify 32-shard test-database USED_BYTES backfill\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T11-18-11-HAhd-yopu_im_message_collection_used_bytes_quota_fix_and_backfill.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-2026-08-20T19-18-11-01a01ee4-93b1-7932-873a-261aceb63f03.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T11:36:39+00:00, thread_id=01a01ee4-93b1-7932-873a-261aceb63f03, success: 32-shard backfill executed; mismatch=0)\n\n### keywords\n\n- TB_MESSAGE_COLLECTION_QUOTA, MEDIA_BYTES, READY, 32 分片, 消息收藏配额_USED_BYTES_回填.sql, 172.21.131.79, 139.196.23.165, releaseUsed, mismatch\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user supplied a closed root cause and asked “要我按这个方案直接改吗？①③ 涉及代码 + ② 需要执行到 test 库” -> directly implement the smallest contract-aligned change, run the backfill, and verify; do not regress to a design discussion, and report code changes versus test-database writes separately. [Task 1][Task 2]\n- when the user cited “physicalBytes 为最终大小；IM 按它结算全局物理容量与用户逻辑配额” -> use the contract document as the repair authority, not a surface workaround. [Task 1]\n- when the user specified “② 需要执行到 test 库” -> confirm access path and shard semantics, make a read-only precheck, then write and immediately verify both the target user and all shards. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- The 0B root cause was a semantic mismatch: image/video content has no `size`, while `CollectionSnapshotBuilder.extractSize()` recognizes only `size/fileSize/bytes`; therefore reservation and used bytes could be 0. `MediaCopyResult.Snapshot.physicalBytes` is available after copy completion and `markReady` writes `MEDIA_BYTES`, so completion-time user quota must settle final physical bytes, consistent with `settlePhysical`. [Task 1]\n- Do not merely replace `reservedBytes` with `totalBytes`: estimated > final leaves too much `RESERVED_BYTES`, and reservation=0/final>0 skips atomic capacity enforcement. Use `convertReservedToUsed(userId,count,reservedBytes,finalBytes)`: add `finalBytes`, subtract only `reservedBytes` with `GREATEST`, and enforce `USED_BYTES + GREATEST(RESERVED_BYTES-reservedBytes,0)+finalBytes <= QUOTA_BYTES` in the same update. Text uses `(0L,0L)`. [Task 1]\n- `completeMediaTask` rejects each snapshot over `maxSingleFileBytes` as `FILE_TOO_LARGE`; zero rows updated means `QUOTA_BYTES_EXCEEDED`. Both are permanent Worker outcomes and must `failAndCleanup`, not retry. Focused command passed 15 tests: `mvn -pl yopu-im/yopu-im-core -am test \"-Dtest=MessageCollectionTaskPersistenceServiceTest,CollectionSnapshotBuilderTest\" \"-DfailIfNoTests=false\" \"-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false\"`; package also passed. [Task 1]\n- Backfill authority is `USED_BYTES = SUM(MEDIA_BYTES)` from READY collection rows per shard; keep `RESERVED_BYTES` unchanged, matching deletion `releaseUsed`. Use `yopu-im/yopu-im-core/src/main/resources/sql/dml/消息收藏配额_USED_BYTES_回填.sql`; success requires an all-shard `USED_BYTES <> COALESCE(READY SUM(MEDIA_BYTES),0)` mismatch count of 0. [Task 2]\n- Only verified test DB access was jump host `139.196.23.165` (db-server01) to `172.21.131.79:3306`; local machine and dev nodes could not connect. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- A large patch failed because the expected Worker context was inaccurate -> apply small focused patches and reread each target before patching. [Task 1]\n- Local PyMySQL timed out and SSH to `10.168.1.232` was rejected -> never report a backfill as executed until a reachable jump host performs it and post-write verification succeeds. [Task 2]\n- Inline multiline `python -c` in PowerShell broke quoting/newlines -> use uploaded SQL with remote mysql, or assemble one remote command string. [Task 1][Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / yopu-crm-account friend authorization snapshot async repair and delete-friend latency diagnosis\nscope: Review, implement, test, and runtime-