ion delete-friend root cause, implement async snapshots, and dev-verify\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n\n### keywords\n\n- deleteFriend, POST /v1/user/social/friend/delete, FRIEND, FRIEND_VIEW, CacheInvalidationOutboxWriter, imSnapshotExecutor, afterCommit, 661171e9-8c51-408a-8c2a-2ec7a44c1bb9, 376 tests, 10.168.1.233:9001\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user asked for “方案评审”, then “补强后评审”, then “你来补强” -> first do a strict document-only review; once asked, directly rewrite the design document rather than waiting for the user to edit it. [Task 1]\n- when asking “改动范围大吗” and “生产才800用户不到，就会卡那么长时间” -> state change size/risk and explain the concrete latency mechanism; do not equate a small user count with a fast request. [Task 1]\n- when the user said “我改完了，是否通过测试” -> compare the diff with the approved design, then run module tests plus a clean rebuild rather than relying on incremental compilation. [Task 1]\n- when the user said “删除好友，大约3-5秒” and “排查一下” -> begin with a no-data-change investigation (metrics, health, source call chain), not by deleting test relations or changing data. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- `acceptFriendRequest` afterCommit work was still in the HTTP thread: about 18 DB plus 20 Redis round trips for two authorization rebuilds, two friend views, fence/JetCache clearing, and Outbox state. Keep the fix narrow: a dedicated `imSnapshotExecutor` (4/8/500/`AbortPolicy`), only FRIEND afterCommit work uses `submitFriendRebuild`, and `RejectedExecutionException` leaves an Outbox fallback; other Outbox types stay synchronous. [Task 1]\n- Do not reuse `accountAsyncExecutor`: its 2/5/200 `CallerRunsPolicy` can return slow rebuild to the request thread. `immediateRebuildFriend` returns success and only then runs `afterSnapshotReady`; welcome messages require snapshots rebuilt and fences cleared first, otherwise REDIS_ONLY `authorizeSingleChat` returns `AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE` and messages can be silently lost. [Task 1]\n- Outbox is fixed-delay 60s with claim/lease and retry, so “60s 内必达” is not hard acceptance; use `outbox_pending_oldest_seconds<120s`, `FAILED=0`, and rejection count 0. Diff matched the design; module then clean test passed 357 and later suite reached 360. [Task 1]\n- Production trace evidence closed the diagnosis: `deleteFriend` registered 1× FRIEND plus 2× FRIEND_VIEW rebuilds as serial synchronous `afterCommit` work in the HTTP thread; the two FRIEND_VIEW rebuilds dominated (~0.94s), making account deletions average ~2.69s. Private cancel (~11.5ms) and IM clear (~7.5ms) were not the cause. [Task 3]\n- The implemented boundary is a dedicated configurable `imSnapshotExecutor` (default core/max/queue `4/8/500`, `AbortPolicy`): FRIEND and FRIEND_VIEW rebuilds are submitted after commit; rejection logs and leaves the Outbox PENDING for compensation instead of falling back to the request thread. Keep immediate JetCache friend-list eviction synchronous for read-after-write consistency. [Task 3]\n- The welcome message may run only after snapshot rebuild, fence clearing, and Outbox COMPLETED; use `afterSnapshotReady`, not the transaction callback itself. Dev real-chain test (login → request → accept → delete → list) showed 97–124ms deletes, immediate empty lists on both sides, and no `AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE`/queue-full/welcome-send failures. Production still needs 3–5 smoke samples ≤300ms and ≥20-request P95 before release. [Task 3]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- The initial plan made all seven Outbox categories asynchronous and did not preserve welcome-message/snapshot order -> minimize the async surface and model cross-thread order explicitly. [Task 1]\n- Earlier dev-only metrics could not prove the 3–5s production report. Pivot to production read-only evidence: the later same-trace log timeline closed the cause without mutating data; where `mysql` is absent, do not invent Outbox state beyond trace evidence. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\n- Large Maven output was truncated -> continue via streaming `write_stdin(session_id)` rather than treating a truncated response as the result. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / yopu-im-core Redis authorization RBatch concurrency risk and reproduction plan\nscope: Assess whether authorization snapshot reads should become concurrent/asynchronous, distinguish supported RBatch evidence from unproven claims, and prepare a safe preproduction reproduction plan.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=test commit, Redis addresses, and live pool configuration are environment-specific; fail-closed authorization and evidence-tier rules are reusable.\n\n## Task 1: Assess authorization-reader async risk and test-branch Batch evidence\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T05-49-30-zy3T-im_redis_batch_concurrency_risk_assessment_and_plan_doc.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-2026-08-20T13-49-30-01a01db7-a702-74d2-ac1c-a97173e1b791.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T06:13:40+00:00, thread_id=01a01db7-a702-74d2-ac1c-a97173e1b791, success: read-only assessment and documented reproduction plan; no production-code change)\n\n### keywords\n\n- RelationAuthorizationSnapshotReader, RBatch, createBatch, BatchOptions.defaults, executeAsync, CommandDecoder, MessageAckService, fail-closed, FENCE_RETRY_DELAYS_MS, c5dcdcfd\n\n## Task 2: Define preproduction mixed-load reproduction and conditional severity\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T05-49-30-zy3T-im_redis_batch_concurrency_risk_assessment_and_plan_doc.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-2026-08-20T13-49-30-01a01db7-a702-74d2-ac1c-a97173e1b791.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T06:13:40+00:00, thread_id=01a01db7-a702-74d2-ac1c-a97173e1b791, suc