ementation and do not split all services at once. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Phase 0 is design-only: freeze boundaries, field-level single-write matrix, V1 contracts/reliable events, rollback switches, observability, reconciliation, and fault/contract tests. It does not create or deploy new services; only P0-01 through P0-03 may start, while P0-04 code refactoring is not authorized. [Task 1]\n- Target eight logical boundaries are Gateway/Access/Store/Deliver-ACK/Session/Push/Group/Relation. The first physical split is Access, Store, Deliver-ACK, Session, and Push; Group/Relation remains the CRM authority domain (`yopu-crm-account`) and IM reads it through Feign/Redis authorization snapshots rather than copying the relation master database. [Task 1]\n- Preserve four invariants: Store alone writes message facts; a conversation orders by canonical `sessionId` while `shardUid` is DB routing only; Store local transactions emit recoverable Reply/Delivery/Session results; `cmd=6` is `ORIGIN_CONNECTION_ONLY` and delivery cannot depend on the origin node surviving. For shared-hot-DB migration, enumerate old writer/new writer/switch/rollback writer per field; a shadow path records differences but never writes. [Task 1]\n- Conditional-pass blockers: client/server must confirm original-connection `cmd=6`, group receive command and ACK rules; DBA must approve session sequencing, durable idempotency and Result Outbox schema/index/retention; MQ/ops must confirm RabbitMQ topology, Confirm/Return/retry/DLQ, partition migration and high watermarks; lock a baseline after assigning existing uncommitted changes; define Snowflake workerId unique lease/renewal/collision stop before Access pre-generates IDs. [Task 1]\n- Physical sequence: first Store (Session Worker co-deployed), then Deliver/ACK, then core converges to Access, then Session/Push; Group/Relation migration is a separate data project with single-write authority, historical migration, Outbox catch-up, dual-read checks, API cutover, and old-entry shutdown. [Task 1]\n- Current limits to account for: ordinary group delivery has no transactional Delivery Outbox (`buildAndSendGroupDeliveryEvent` sends after commit), carries full `recipientUserIds`, uses 8 fixed partitions, writes every member's Session Index, and ACK retry scans Redis Pending Keys under one global lock. Capacity evidence remains contextual: acceptance redline is `cmd5==cmd6==cmd27==cmd7`, zero lost/duplicate/out_of_order/ackPending, and MQ/Result/Session Outboxes drained. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Treating multi-device idempotency as `clientType` alone can collide for two devices of the same type -> lock a real `recipientEndpointKey` during P0-01. [Task 1]\n- Do not use “dual-node throughput nearly doubles” as a split or Phase 0 gate. It is only a post-split capacity observation; cross-node message correctness remains the release redline. [Task 1]\n- A compiling module is not proof that `chatDbAsyncExecutor` is safely injected: `IMServiceImpl` expects `RejectingExecutor`, while its Bean signature returns `Executor`/`ThreadPoolTaskExecutor` -> require context startup and saturated-queue tests. Run `git diff --check` for plan edits; use quoted/LiteralPath PowerShell handling for Chinese paths. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / sprint test branch CRM local build, startup, and shutdown\nscope: Repair a broken local `test`-branch Maven build, start `yopu-crm-account` without registering a personal instance in shared Nacos, verify health, and stop only the target process.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\sprint\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=this is a distinct sprint checkout; commits, uncommitted fixes, services, ports, and dev endpoints are time-sensitive, while the build and PowerShell shields are reusable.\n\n## Task 1: Repair the local WIP build and start yopu-crm-account\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-24T10-04-58-3EK3