ks \"是不是opencodex或者其他导致我的codex卡呢\" -> treat OpenCodex as an independent hypothesis and separate proxy/response-delay evidence from UI-rendering and local-index evidence. [Task 1]\n- when the user asks \"有没有时间长不用的会话，帮我归档或者删除\" -> default to reversible archiving rather than deletion; explain the difference and preserve pinned, running, and currently relevant work. [Task 2]\n- when the user says \"你直接帮我优化\" after diagnosis is clear -> execute the smallest-risk optimization directly rather than prolonging analysis or asking again. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- For UI/task-opening slowness, inspect active `sessions` JSONL size and `C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\logs_2.sqlite` before blaming model/network latency. In this verified run, a 4.32GB active-session set and a 1.10GB log database were stronger suspects than OpenCodex; a small current task did not rule out global-index cost. [Task 1]\n- Oversized session space was highly concentrated: seven >=100MB files held about 86% of 4.22GB, mainly image-generation work. Prioritize a few large sessions rather than many <10MB sessions. [Task 2]\n- `C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\config.toml` showed OpenCodex routing through `openai_base_url = \"http://127.0.0.1:10100/v1\"`; `netstat -ano` followed by a PID-filtered process query confirmed bun/OpenCodex on 10100. This proxy can affect response/send delay, but is not the leading explanation for task-opening/UI lag. [Task 1]\n- `codex_app__list_threads` accepts at most `limit:50`; inspect `pinnedThreads` and active `threads`, then archive using `codex_app__set_thread_archived({threadId, hostId:\"local\", archived:true})` and verify the task is absent from the active list. Archiving moves JSONL from `sessions\\` to `archived_sessions\\`; it does not shrink `logs_2.sqlite`. [Task 2]\n- A safe successful intervention archived six oversized image/content tasks, reducing active sessions from 135 / 4.32GB to 129 / 0.81GB while retaining the current task, running work, pinned tasks, and