 cleared or record its baseline, then verify 47 health, the deployed JMeter file, and current process configuration. Historical backlog-induced `cmd=27` delay is not a capacity result for the new run. [Task 3]\n- `im_single_chat_duplex_continuous.jmx` uses one long-lived JDK 17 WebSocket per real user; users both send and receive, targets are mapped after login, and the final summary records cmd=5/6/27/7, QPS/TPS, P50/P95/P99, delivery/ACK rate, loss, duplicates, and ordering. `users.json` has only 500 valid users, so larger runs require more real credentials and friend mappings. [Task 1]\n- The validated cross-host P0 used 165=`139.196.23.165`/`172.20.196.192` as the JMeter pressure host and 47=`47.116.106.227`/`172.20.196.193` as the IM server. With two users at one message/user/second for 30 seconds, `cmd=5/6/27/7=60/60/60/60`, delivery/ACK were 100%, and loss/duplicates/out-of-order were zero: P0 only, not a capacity result. [Task 2]\n- `SingleChatPerformanceObserver` localized the gap to business execution through local Netty push write: cmd=6 P50/P95/P99=`489/504/748ms`, cmd=27=`449/459/663ms`, queued-to-executing is near zero, pushWritten is about 441–452ms, and pushWritten-to-ACK about 3–5ms. Add segmented timing across persistence, routing, MQ publish/confirm, MQ consumer, and push before altering fixed pool sizes; socket writes remain on the channel EventLoop. [Task 2]\n\n- For the 2000-user three-host run, shard 165=1200, 75=500, 89=300 without overlap and confirm each shard has local online-friend targets. `allLoginTimeoutMs` must exceed the login ramp; 240s ramp with a 180s gate timed out, while a 360s gate passed login. Capacity acceptance requires login, business, final protocol aggregate, and MQ/Outbox tail together. [Task 4]\n- The 2026-08-03 three-host result is not a capacity pass: `cmd5=60000`, `cmd6/cmd27=59998`, `cmd7=59786` (2 missing messages and 212 ACK gap); MQ/Outbox tail was not verified. The 165-only run also cannot support a strict 2000 msg/s claim because staggered login compressed send time (`cmd5=57172`, `cmd6/cmd27=57167`, `cmd7=57165`). Rework the JMX into a two-stage model with shared `businessStartAt` and a fixed 30s business window after all users log in. [Task 4]\n- `IMHandler.handleMessageDeliverAck()` had marked receipt without `MessageAckService.confirmAck(userId,msgId)`, leaving Redis pending keys and enabling duplicate direct pushes. The repair calls `confirmAck` for `cmd=7`; `IMServiceImpl` and `MessageConsumer` register pending before WebSocket write and cancel it on write failure; retry exhaustion/offline delivery uses idempotent `OfflineMessagePersistenceService.persist` before clearing pending/retry keys. `MessageAckService` defaults observed in source: pending TTL 300s, max retry 3, Redis-key scan retry. Package validation (`mvn -pl yopu-im/yopu-im-core -am package \"-Dmaven.test.skip=true\"`) and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 5]\n- The matrix script is `im_single_chat_duplex_continuous_codex.jmx`. A short-window result is acceptable only when login, business-send, final-summary, four-command closure, and MQ/Outbox tail all pass. `matrix-1500-rerun-20260803` met `1500/0` for main samples with MQ `ready/unack/consumers=0/0/8` and Outbox zero; retain the earlier 1000 login and 1500 business failures as variability/reliability evidence. [Task 6]\n- `matrix-2000-20260803` used 2000 threads, 240s ramp, 30s business window, and 330s duration after zero MQ/Outbox gates. Nineteen users did not reach a 180s login barrier; `IM_LOGIN_CONNECT 1981/0` was followed by `IM_BUSINESS_CONTINUOUS_SEND 1981/1981`. This is a load-generator/readiness failure, not a valid 2000-user IM-throughput result. [Task 6]\n- C0/C1 single-variable evidence identifies `TB_USER_SESSION_INDEX` UPSERT as the current 1000-QPS bottleneck: disabling it changed cmd6 P50/P95 from 17.9s/39.4s to 69ms/108ms, restored about 999.8/s persistence, and reduced lock waits 99.7%. P1-A batch-local merge/sort by `(USER_ID, SESSION_ID)` reduces one-batch contention but is not cross-consumer key serialization. [Task 8]\n- P1-A is not accepted: business P50/P95 was 40/56ms but Outbox unapplied was 96,146 (53%); same-key cross-batch/cross-consumer UPSERT contention remained. Use fixed-key partition serialization and bounded batching only after real P1-B load evidence. [Task 8]\n- Scheme B: `ChatDbBatchDispatcher` aggregates 50ms, groups `SHARD_UID % 32`, and defaults to an 8-thread per-shard executor; `ChatDbBatchProperties.enabled=false`. `ChatDbBatchPersistService` writes messages and matching Outbox in one transaction, retries only routing/deadlock errors, then uses row-wise idempotent fallback. Watch `[IM-CHATDB-BATCH]` and `[IM-THREADPOOL]`; pre-production 96/128-thread settings do not validate production 24/48 with `chat-db=false`. [Task 8]\n- `dev-im-merge` is a production candidate baseline (thread/MQ isolation, bounded queues, `AbortPolicy`, optional CPU affinity); `dev-imtest` is the stricter real-user JMeter/closed-loop observability system. Production-safe single-chat priorities are: `RBatch` for login/heartbeat while preserving routing/online/TTL semantics, move heartbeat Redis work off Netty workers and return explicit failure ACK on rejection, offline/DLQ fallback with `NACK(requeue=false)`, then minimize the persistence/session-index transaction. Async DB needs durable compensation and 500/1000-user A/B before enablement; CPU affinity/pool expansion are later experiments. [Task 9]\n- Verified chain: Netty decode/auth -> `messageProcessor` authorization precheck -> `SingleChatPersistenceTask` on `chatDbAsyncExecutor` / `im-asyncdb-` -> message main table plus session Outbox in the `saveSingleMessage` transaction -> local synchronous push or cross-node MQ (offline only when no online route) -> cmd6 ACK. The session index uses 16 serial partitions, 150 records/50ms aggregation, ledger deduplication, batch upsert, and post-commit cache invalidation. Source-default Outbox polling is 100ms but Nacos can override it at runtime. [Task 10]\n- The five-node 200 QPS x 120s run (23,994 messages) closed at aggregate 1000 QPS only; it cannot establish 2000 QPS or validate a high-single-host connection model. Use 1500 QPS x 180s for three all-zero rounds -> 2000 QPS x 180s -> 2000 QPS x 10min for three all-zero rounds, with `CallerRuns=0`, stable P99, and no sustained MySQL/Redis/MQ saturation. [Task 10]\n- Prioritize bounded queues with fast rejection/explicit busy metrics over `CallerRunsPolicy`, restore transactional persistent `(senderId, clientMsgId)` idempotency that returns the first `messageId`, then add segmented cmd6 metrics before tuning pools. Local synchronous push may reduce cmd27 but occupies `im-asyncdb-`; test the proposed independent bounded delivery executor with A/B evidence before claiming throughput gains. [Task 10]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Do not run directly when queue status, 47 health, JMeter artifact, or process configuration is unknown; do not attribute an old queue backlog to the new run's capacity. [Task 3]\n- `DuplexListener` cannot read outer JMeter `props`: `groovy.lang.MissingPropertyException: No such property: props for class: DuplexListener` -> pass command configuration through shared listener state. [Task 1]\n- A failed early smoke can be a script/runtime issue, not an IM performance result: inspect JTL `responseMessage` and `listenerError` first. For restarts, verify actual PID, 8084/8085, health, and `/actuator/beans` wiring for `singleChatPerformanceObserver`, not only the JAR filename. [Task 2]\n- `--spring.cloud.nacos.enabled=false` does not reliably suppress Nacos ConfigData import; a known recovery path explicitly supplies `--spring.config.import=optional:file:/opt/yopu-apps/conf/application-pre.yaml`, then verifies service health. Monitor RSS, Direct Memory, GC, and OOM before high-connection tests on 47 because `-Xmx50g + MaxDirectMemorySize=10g` leaves little headroom on 64G. [Task 2]\n- Do not call a run passed solely because all users logged in or a sender-side total looks complete. Require `cmd5 == cmd6 == cmd27 == cmd7 == planned`, zero loss/duplicate/out-of-order, `ackPending=0`, and MQ/Outbox tail completion. [Task 4]\n- Do not claim the new ACK/offline tests passed: existing `IMServiceImplTest.java:[119,33]` and `[121,34]` fail test compilation because `isRetryableShardingRouteException(IllegalStateException)` is missing. Remaining risks: offline-persistence failure retains only pending TTL, ACK misses are DEBUG-only, Redis full scans can cause retry bursts, and long JMeter runs do not reclaim `sent/byContent` maps. In PowerShell, quote whole Maven `-D` arguments. [Task 5]\n- When a 2000 run has incomplete login at the barrier, do not call the downstream business errors an IM capacity failure. Increase/parameterize `allLoginTimeoutMs` beyond ramp/readiness, ensure every login thread can reach the barrier, and collect target CPU/RSS/GC/EventLoop/connection and JMeter metrics before retrying. Do not begin 3000 until 2000 closes the full protocol and MQ/Outbox gates. [Task 6]\n- Do not equate MySQL global cumulative `Innodb_row_lock_waits` or `setAutoCommit -> socket read` with this run's row-lock cause: capture `BUSINESS_START/END` deltas and correlate `data_lock_waits`, `data_locks`, and `processlist`. `BUSINESS_END` and `DRAIN_END` are separate; final queue=0 is not a steady-window pass. [Task 8]\n- The new `SessionIndexPartitionDispatcher` initially appeared patched but its file was absent -> after adding files, run `Test-Path`/`Get-Item` before compiling. Its Maven package passed only with `-Dmaven.test.skip=true`; no P1-B load result exists. For a targeted reactor test, quote `\"-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false\"`; a normal `-DskipTests` build was blocked by existing `IMServiceImplTest` missing-method compilation. [Task 8]\n- Static branch comparison is not a JMeter/service/capacity run. Long Chinese paths can make `git show` fail; prefer short paths, `git diff --stat`, class-name search, or the working-tree file. Do not promote virtual users, auth bypasses, or virtual group members into production paths. [Task 9]\n- Do not treat local synchronous push's lower cmd27 as a throughput gain: first measure its long-lived occupancy of `im-asyncdb-` and the full protocol closure. If high single-host connection tests show duplicate/ACK-pending noise on Java HttpClient `SelectorManager`, distribute load generators and repair the login ramp/barrier before attributing readiness failure to the IM server. [Task 10]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM message-quote protocol and acceptance design\nscope: Review and document the server-side message-quote contract, persistence, invalidation, and compatibility rules; this rollout did not implement business code.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=recheck ImCommandConstant, IMHandler, gateway contracts, and the approved document before implementation.\n\n## Task 1: Review and update the message-quote implementation/acceptance plan\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-30T07-11-07-7Fmu-im_message_quote_plan_review_and_protocol_update.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\30\\rollout-2026-07-30T15-11-07-019fb1dc-d31f-7872-b0b5-901078c5226e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-30T09:31:48+00:00, thread_id=019fb1dc-d31f-7872-b0b5-901078c5226e, success: design document reviewed and updated)\n\n### keywords\n\n- content + extra + mentions, extra.replyTo.messageId, /v1/im/message/quote/target, ImCommandConstant, IMHandler, cmd=5, cmd=6, cmd=11, cmd=12, cmd=22, cmd=27, QUOTE_MESSAGE_ID, QUOTE_STATUS, MESSAGE_EXTRA, outbox\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user asked “具体要提供几个接口给客户端” -> state the count of new client APIs, changed existing contracts, command matrix, and acceptance evidence directly. [Task 1]\n- when the user asked “补强后评审” and adopted `content + extra + mentions` -> expose blockers first, then make the user's protocol the contract and strengthen server validation/state consistency around it. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- The approved shape is `content + extra + mentions`: client uploads only `extra.replyTo.messageId`; server generates the quote snapshot/status/version and returns `extra.replyTo` consistently in ACK, push, and history. `extra` needs version, whitelist, and size validation; reject or strip unknown fields. `mentions` remains a separate executable-semantic field, with no @ business expansion this phase. [Task 1]\n- Protocol directions: single uplink `cmd=5`, ACK `cmd=6`; group uplink `cmd=11`, ACK/push `cmd=12`; single receive push `cmd=27`; revoke/quote invalidation `cmd=22`. String fast paths `handleSingleChat(String)` and `handleGroupChat(String)` must parse nested `extra.replyTo.messageId`; use DTO + `ObjectMapper`, not hand-written JSON. [Task 1]\n- Add one original-message-location HTTP API, `/v1/im/message/quote/target`; the other four are existing payload-contract changes, not five new APIs. Gateway `/v1/im/**` injects identity; never trust a client `userId`. Persist indexed `QUOTE_MESSAGE_ID`, `QUOTE_STATUS`, snapshot, and state version rather than scanning `MESSAGE_EXTRA`. [Task 1]\n- Revoke/cleanup is a separate cmd=22 `event` with `eventId`, `rootMessageId`, `stateVersion`, chunked affected quote IDs, `sequence`, and `lastChunk`; clients process idempotently. Keep hot-store updates atomic; use outbox/compensation for cold store and ES rather than promising a global transaction. Capability downgrade must cover WebSocket, HTTP history/offline pull, and device Push. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Do not confuse uplink, ACK, receive push, and revoke event; verify `ImCommandConstant.java` and `IMHandler` before writing the command matrix. [Task 1]\n- Do not mark all system messages non-quotable