s\\Fiddler2` and `C:\\Users\\79873\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Fiddler`. `Fiddler Everywhere` winget downloads can hang; if needed, stop only the stuck winget and resume with `curl.exe -L --continue-at -` plus SHA256, but do not mistake it for the final working capture tool. [Task 1]\n- Mixed PowerShell/adb/shell quoting breaks `%{http_code}` and nested braces; wrap the remote command in double quotes from PowerShell. `toybox nc -z` is unsupported; use `echo | toybox nc -w 3 host port`. Keep `CustomRules.js` minimal: a compile error silently disables all rules. [Task 2][Task 3]\n- Do not claim WebSocket capture from a listener or long TCP connection: require fresh `101 Switching Protocols` plus frames. In the CMD repair script do not put `<-` in echo text because CMD treats `<` as redirection; invoke `cmd /c '...\\fix_fiddler_proxy.cmd'` without `< nul` from PowerShell. [Task 3]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IMServiceImpl benchmark bypass and Locust single-chat testing\nscope: Plan or implement a reproducible single-chat benchmark that retains the formal IM send path and MySQL persistence while suppressing Redis/Feign only within the controlled send branch.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=checkout-specific call-chain/line facts and partial design evidence; do not claim throughput, P99, or capacity until a real target-server run validates the counters and recipient delivery.\n\n## Task 1: Retain the formal IMHandler → IMServiceImpl send path for benchmarking\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-25T05-44-12-8wAs-imserviceimpl_locust_single_chat_benchmark_redesign.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\25\\rollout-2026-07-25T13-44-12-019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-25T08:55:16+00:00, thread_id=019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04, partial: redesign/analysis completed; no target-server benchmark result)\n\n### keywords\n\n- IMHandler.handleSingleChat, IMServiceImpl.sendSingleMessage, BenchmarkMessagePath, Redis, Feign, MySQL, checkIdempotent, deliverMessageToUser, CallerRunsPolicy\n\n## Task 2: Evaluate and redesign Locust single-chat testing\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-25T05-44-12-8wAs-imserviceimpl_locust_single_chat_benchmark_redesign.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\25\\rollout-2026-07-25T13-44-12-019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-25T08:55:16+00:00, thread_id=019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04, partial: current script assessed; strict end-to-end redesign remains pending)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Locust, locustfile_single.py, users_*.json, WebSocket, cmd=1, cmd=5, cmd=27, fixed-pairing, success=false, result-500.html\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when performance work begins, the user asked “先给出方案 md” -> inspect code facts and provide a reviewable plan before modifying business code or running a load test. [Task 1]\n- when the first benchmark bypassed the business service, the user corrected: “为什么不去 imserviceImpl 实现类中把第三方调用来源禁用掉呢” -> benchmark the formal `IMHandler → IMServiceImpl` send path; bare Netty/in-memory Channel is only a secondary baseline. [Task 1]\n- the user said “只要保证在发送消息的时候目前不走 Redis、不调 Feign 就行” and “落库保留” -> constrain bypasses to send-stage Redis/Feign; retain MySQL message persistence/conversation update and keep any no-DB run as a separately labelled baseline. [Task 1]\n- when the user said “我先测单聊” and asked how the script works -> start with standalone, reproducible single-chat Locust instructions and clearly distinguish the load-generator host from the target IM service. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Formal single-chat entry: `IMHandler.handleSingleChat` → `IMServiceImpl.sendSingleMessage`; group entry: `handleGroupChat` → `sendGroupMessage`. The current send path also contains idempotency Redis, sender-profile cache, authorization through `RelationAuthorizationSnapshotReader` or `SendPrecheckFeignClient`, Redis routing/MQ/offline delivery, conversation cache, stranger limits, and moderation. [Task 1]\n- A valid persistence-retaining benchmark keeps message object/ID construction, MySQL or sharded write, and formal response; it bypasses only the controlled Redis/Feign/cache/authorization/routing/remote-MQ/offline-push/unread/conversation-cache/moderation side paths, with local online Channel delivery. Verify branch hit count, MySQL writes, local deliveries, and Redis/Feign/MQ/offline call counters all together. [Task 1]\n- Group benchmark recipient lists originate from Redis authorization snapshots or Feign `getSendAuthorizationSnapshot`; if that source is bypassed, load a fixed local member snapshot rather than merely removing authorization. [Task 1]\n- `locustfile_single.py` loads `users_*.json`, opens formal WebSockets, logs in with `cmd=1`, sends single chat with `cmd=5`, and keeps heartbeat/reconnect behavior. Run `locust -f locustfile_single.py --web-host 0.0.0.0 --web-port 8090`; a headless example is `locust -f locustfile_single.py --headless -u 500 -r 50 --run-time 10m --html result-500.html`. [Task 2]\n- Current script is not a strict capacity test: it selects among 100 ring targets with 40/40/20 activity waits and only observes sender response. Use fixed pairs, explicit send rate, pre-exported JSON data, receiver `cmd=27` accounting, and loss/duplicate/out-of-order metrics for comparable 500/800/1000/2000/5000-user runs. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- `BenchmarkMessagePath` measured only Netty plus an in-memory Channel because it bypassed `IMServiceImpl`; first lock down which layer is being measured, then implement a controlled branch in that layer. [Task 1]\n- Commenting a stranger-rate-limit step does not remove all external calls. Do not use `ss` alone as