en propose remediation separately. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- `CommandDispatcher.dispatch()` is called from `IMHandler.channelRead0()` and directly invokes login, chat, read-ack, revoke, reconnect, and call handlers; no business-executor handoff was found before these calls. [Task 1]\n- The login path synchronously does JWT validation, Redis route refresh, Redisson connection/cache work, DB conversation lookup, Feign user/group lookup, and offline-message DB read/delete plus Redis counter update. `ConversationServiceImpl.getRecentConversationList()` waits with `CompletableFuture.allOf(...).get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS)` and reads Redis per conversation. [Task 1]\n- `ConnectionManagerImpl` uses synchronous Redisson bucket reads/writes; per-conversation cache updates add linear Redis round trips. Single/group send handlers directly invoke transactional `sendSingleMessage` / `sendGroupMessage`, including Redis, database, and in some modes synchronous Feign authorization. [Task 1]\n- `ModerationQueueConfig.groupInfoQueryExecutor` uses `CallerRunsPolicy`; saturation can run blocking Feign work on the submitting EventLoop. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Static review did not run a benchmark, slow-dependency injection, or EventLoop metrics; do not quantify production P99 impact from this evidence alone. [Task 1]\n- Do not async-wrap only one Feign call. Move the complete business command to a bounded business executor with fast rejection/degradation, avoid `CallerRunsPolicy` fallback to EventLoop, and add EventLoop pending-task, command-duration, dependency-P99, and rejection metrics. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM relation separation, Redis-only cutover, and warmup scheduling\nscope: Keep relations authoritative in CRM Account, plan a fail-closed Redis-only authorization cutover, and stagger repair warmups; the rollout is design/acceptance evidence, not production validation.\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=recheck branch `dev-imtest`, Account/IM contracts, Redis state, and runtime topology; test/compile evidence does not replace middleware and real-client acceptance.\n\n## Task 1: Design and review friend/group relation separation implementation and acceptance plan\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-18T03-10-12-ETuk-im_relation_separation_redis_only_pressure_test_and_cron.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07-18T11-10-17-019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T12:11:48+00:00, thread_id=019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4, success: design review passed; real-environment acceptance not run)\n\n### keywords\n\n- TB_FRIEND_RELATION, TB_GROUP_INFO, TB_GROUP_USER_RELATION, yopu-crm-account, SocialInternalFeignClient, fail-closed, groupMemberCheck, Outbox, P0/P1/P2\n\n## Task 2: Plan direct Redis-only authorization cutover\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-18T03-10-12-ETuk-im_relation_separation_redis_only_pressure_test_and_cron.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07-18T11-10-17-019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T12:11:48+00:00, thread_id=019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4, success: direct cutover procedure designed)\n\n### keywords\n\n- yopu.im.auth.running-mode=redis_only, TB_RELATION_CACHE_INVALIDATION_OUTBOX, /user/internal/job/im-auth-warmup/users, failedCount=0, yopu:im:warmup:failed:*, feign rollback\n\n## Task 3: Stagger the five Redis warmup jobs\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-18T03-10-12-ETuk-im_relation_separation_redis_only_pressure_test_and_cron.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived