invalid binding, but bulk requests cannot identify it precisely. [Task 1]\n- Different dev/prod source AppKey fingerprints reduce accidental cross-delivery, but Nacos can override runtime configuration. A real cross-environment proof requires uninstall-prod -> install-dev -> bind/login -> send from production, plus Nacos, AppKey/package, binding endpoint, and Redis checks. [Task 1]\n- For Pre cleanup, remove both the `push:device:user:{userId}` Hash field and matching `push:device:reg:{registrationId}` reverse key; a full cleanup must use batched Redis `SCAN`, never `KEYS`, after Pre offline Push is disabled. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Do not stop `im-core` or ordinary message MQ consumers to disable offline Push; that can affect normal chat delivery. `@RefreshScope` does not prove all listener concurrency/config refreshes take effect: verify Nacos refresh, new-task counts, MQ publishes, and JPush logs during rollout. [Task 1]\n- Do not infer production/device behavior from YAML or treat JPush API acceptance as delivery. Low-activity/terminated Android delivery also depends on OEM channels and `POST_NOTIFICATIONS`; iOS must match the APNs production/development environment. [Task 1]\n- Focused validation was `mvn -pl yopu-im/yopu-im-core -am \"-Dtest=OfflinePushTaskAdmissionServiceTest,OfflinePushDispatcherTest,OfflineMessagePersistenceServiceImplTest\" \"-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false\" test`: 12 tests, 0 failures/errors, `BUILD SUCCESS`. This is not live Nacos/RabbitMQ/device acceptance. [Task 1]\n\n# Task Group: aigc-dali-cat / storyboard production and asset governance\nscope: 伪纪录片图文生产编排、锁定资产、storyboard-first 文档、提示词模板合规和浏览器下载约束。\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat; reuse_rule=follow current authority docs and inspect Git/untracked assets first.\n\n## Task 1: 05c asset lock, README V1.1 synchronization, and template-compliant reference-image regeneration\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- roll