ies use `min(60*2^N,3600)` and future `NEXT_RETRY_TIME` records are not scanned. `LEASE_DURATION_SECONDS=120`; acceptance remains `outbox_pending_oldest_seconds<120s` and `FAILED=0`. Safe semantic-preserving accelerators are larger batch, shorter delay, or more instances because `tryClaim` atomically prevents duplicate ownership. [Task 3]\n553:- Symptom: a private-view tombstone looks like a delete-path cleanup defect. Cause: the write/reconcile contract deliberately retains status=0. Fix: inspect the writer and reconciliation semantics before changing data; repair the reader-side visibility filter. [Task 1]\n557:scope: Build source-backed Redis Key inventories using the required business-semantics/Type/Codec/Schema format; review against the codec contract, and deliver a visible all-domain board while preserving the source-vs-runtime boundary.\n911:- when defining the message behavior, the user corrected “方向错了，是A加B，B同意后，给A发消息：你好，我是B ... 且A消息列表1条未读” -> do not invent bilateral system messages; preserve the requested B→A direction and receiver-side unread semantics. [Task 1]\n958:- when the user specified “② 需要执行到 test 库” -> confirm access path and shard semantics, make a read-only precheck, then write and immediately verify both the target user and all shards. [Task 2]\n962:- The 0B root cause was a semantic mismatch: image/video content has no `size`, while `CollectionSnapshotBuilder.extractSize()` recognizes only `size/fileSize/bytes`; therefore reservation and used bytes could be 0. `MediaCopyResult.Snapshot.physicalBytes` is available after copy completion and `markReady` writes `MEDIA_BYTES`, so completion-time user quota must settle final physical bytes, consistent with `settlePhysical`. [Task 1]\n1896:applies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\sprint\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=branch and file paths are checkout-specific; the semantic-gap and acceptance rules are reusable for IM features.\n2264:- `dev-im-merge` is a production candidate baseline (thread/MQ isolation, bounded queues, `AbortPolicy`, optional CPU affinity); `dev-imtest` is the stricter real-user JMeter/closed-loop observability system. Production-safe single-chat priorities are: `RBatch` for login/heartbeat while preserving routing/online/TTL semantics, move heartbeat Redis work off Netty workers and return explicit failure ACK on rejection, offline/DLQ fallback with `NACK(requeue=false)`, then minimize the persistence/session-index transaction. Async DB needs durable compensation and 500/1000-user A/B before enablement; CPU affinity/pool expansion are later experiments. [Task 9]\n2304:- The approved shape is `content + extra + mentions`: client uploads only `extra.replyTo.messageId`; server generates the quote snapshot/status/version and returns `extra.replyTo` consistently in ACK, push, and history. `extra` needs version, whitelist, and size validation; reject or strip unknown fields. `mentions` remains a separate executable-semantic field, with no @ business expansion this phase. [Task 1]\nPath                                                               Lines Chars\r\n----                                                               ----- -----\r\nC:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\skills\\ai-coding-collaboration\\SKILL.md        141  6802\r\nC:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\skills\\douyin-horror-story-pipeline\\SKILL.md   121  8767\r\nSTART_HERE.md                                                        420 12456\r\nSKILL.md                                                             503 17471\r\nconfig\\storyos.yaml                                                  166  4686\r\nconfig\\index.yaml                                                    119  3844\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
