{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.codex\\\\skills\\\\ai-coding-collaboration\\\\SKILL.md' -Raw -Encoding UTF8\n'===== DOUYIN SKILL ====='\nGet-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.codex\\\\skills\\\\douyin-horror-story-pipeline\\\\SKILL.md' -Raw -Encoding UTF8\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: ai-coding-collaboration\ndescription: Use when coding agents need guardrails against overengineering, scope creep, missing validation, noisy handoffs, or unverified completion. Classifies tasks by size, enforces minimal diff, runs impact and self-checks, and ends with concise evidence-based summaries. Trigger for coding tasks, bug fixes, feature work, code review, test/acceptance planning, implementation handoff, or generating project agent rules from the AI Coding execution specification.\n---\n\n# AI Coding Guardrails\n\n## Purpose\n\nApply pragmatic guardrails for AI coding work: classify the task, choose the lightest sufficient process, keep diffs small, validate core behavior, and end with a concise evidence-based summary.\n\nThis skill is packaged as **AI Coding Guardrails**. The repository and Codex skill identifier may still appear as `ai-coding-collaboration` for compatibility.\n\nFor the full source specification, read `references/ai-coding-execution-spec-v1.md` when the user asks for the complete standard, wants to generate derived rule files, or the task is ambiguous enough that the condensed rules below are insufficient. That specification is normative; prompts and examples are supporting material.\n\n## Task Level Decision\n\nChoose the lowest level that safely covers the request:\n\n| Level | Use for | Process |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| L0 micro task | Copy tweaks, small style change, simple bug, single-file fix | Understand -> change -> self-check -> summary |\n| L1 small feature | Simple API, button, form validation, small page change | Task card -> impact analysis -> implement -> checklist -> summary |\n| L2 module task | Login, permissions, payment, uploads, multi-layer backend/frontend/database work | Short plan -> task split -> implement stepwise -> review -> test -> summary |\n| L3 project task | New project, major refactor, core architecture or risky database changes | PRD/architecture/backlog -> stepwise implementation -> release checklist |\n\nDo not run L2/L3 ceremony for L0/L1 work. Do not skip analysis for L2/L3 work.\n\n## Risk Modifiers\n\nTask size is not the only decision. Upgrade the workflow to at least L2 and ask for explicit scope confirmation before implementation when a change affects any of the following:\n\n- authentication, authorization, secrets, or security controls\n- payments, billing, or other irreversible external actions\n- production configuration, data deletion, migrations, or backfills\n- public APIs, shared contracts, or data isolation\n\nState the modifier and the reason for the upgrade. Do not treat a small diff as low risk merely because it changes few lines.\n\n## Ambiguity Gate\n\nFor L2/L3 work, pause before planning when an unresolved product decision, acceptance criterion, ownership boundary, or irreversible trade-off could change the implementation. Inspect the codebase first, then ask one focused question at a time with a recommended default.\n\nDo not run a grilling session by default for L0/L1 work. If the user has supplied clear acceptance criteria, proceed without extra questions.\n\n## Non-Negotiable Rules\n\n- Analyze complex tasks before proposing a solution, and implement only after scope is clear.\n- Do not make large code changes unless the user asks to implement, modify, or execute.\n- Inspect current code, docs, config, and tests when uncertain.\n- Use the smallest safe diff; avoid unrelated formatting, renames, dependency additions, and opportunistic refactors.\n- Do not rename public APIs, routes, DTOs, database fields, or config keys without explicit scope.\n- Do not delete existing tests unless the reason is stated and replacement coverage is added.\n- Prefer root-cause fixes over surface workarounds.\n- If verification cannot be completed, say exactly what was not verified and why.\n\n## Required Pre-Implementation Checks\n\nFor L1+ implementation, state a compact impact analysis before editing:\n\n```text\nBackend API: yes/no\nService logic: yes/no\nDTO/types: yes/no\nDatabase/config: yes/no\nFrontend page/API call: yes/no\nRouting/navigation: yes/no\nTests/validation: yes/no\nRisk: max 3 bullets\n```\n\nFor L0, skip the table unless the change touches API, database, auth, or user data.\n\n## Implementation Discipline\n\n- Keep changes reversible and scoped to the task.\n- Reuse existing patterns and file organization.\n- Preserve existing behavior unless the user requests a behavior change.\n- Record discovered unrelated issues as follow-up notes instead of fixing them in the same diff.\n- Match the repository's style and command conventions.\n\n## Validation Rules\n\nUse P0/P1/P2 validation instead of long test lists:\n\n- **P0 required**: core flow runs, data is correct, API/page entry works, build/typecheck passes where relevant.\n- **P1 recommended**: empty state, invalid params, duplicate submit, network failure, legacy data.\n- **P2 optional**: performance, large data, extreme UI boundaries, weak-network behavior.\n\nNever mark work as merge-ready when P0 validation was not run or failed. If tests are unavailable, report manual validation or state unverified.\n\n## Validation Evidence\n\nFor every P0 item, report the command or manual path, its result, and any coverage limitation. A statement such as \"tests passed\" without the command or observable result is not validation evidence.\n\n## OpenSpec Cooperation\n\nThis skill governs execution quality; it does not replace persistent change specifications.\n\n- L0/L1: use Guardrails only unless the repository already requires a specification.\n- L2/L3: keep a short decision record. When the repository uses OpenSpec, work through its proposal/apply/archive workflow and use this skill for task level, risk, minimal diff, and validation evidence.\n- Do not create an `openspec/` directory or add a new workflow tool unless the user explicitly requests it.\n\n## Post-Implementation Self-Check\n\nBefore final handoff, answer internally and report material gaps:\n\n1. Is any requested item missing?\n2. Did any code change remain unverified?\n3. Were API, route, DTO, config, database, or test impacts missed?\n4. Are there new risks or follow-up tasks?\n5. Can the work proceed to review, or does it need more changes?\n\n## Review Output\n\nFor code review tasks, use:\n\n```text\nConclusion: merge-ready / can continue / needs small fix / must rework\nBlocker: required fixes\nMajor: important issues\nMinor: optional improvements, max 3\nNext step: direct fix prompt or action\n```\n\nDo not produce broad generic review advice.\n\n## Final Executive Summary\n\nEnd implementation or review turns with a short summary:\n\n```text\n【目标】one sentence\n【改动文件】key files and purpose\n【自测结果】commands/manual checks run\n【风险】max 3\n【必须验收】max 5 items\n【结论】can continue / merge-ready / needs small fix / must rework\n```\n\nKeep it concise. Do not claim merge-ready when there are unverified core paths.\n\r\n===== DOUYIN SKILL =====\r\n---\nname: douyin-horror-story-pipeline\ndescription: Bilingual production workflow for Douyin AI horror/storytelling image posts. Use when the user sends “选题”, “分镜”, “验收”, “自动”, or “对比打分”, or asks to design, storyboard, audit, score, or compare a first-person suspense image-story project using the 鼠鼠传播节奏 + Zayn视觉扩张 mixed mode.\n---\n\n# Douyin Horror Story Pipeline\n\nUse this skill to run a structured, bilingual-capable production pipeline for first-person Douyin suspense/horror image stories. The default project language is Chinese; answer in English when the user explicitly requests English or sends an English command. Keep Chinese command names and S/Z labels unchanged in both languages.\n\n## Authority and references\n\nFor work inside `aigc-dali-cat`, read the repository authority documents before making judgments:\n\n- `standards/制作规范_正式版.md`\n- The relevant episode `README.md`, docs, assets README, storyboard, publish checklist, and review files\n- `shushu/` and `zayn/` only when competitor-sample evidence is needed; treat them as local samples, not universal platform rules\n\nLoad the detailed language reference only as needed:\n\n- Chinese workflow: `references/zh-CN.md`\n- English workflow: `references/en-US.md`\n\nDo not invent missing source facts. Mark assumptions as assumptions. Preserve the distinction between a design score, a pre-publish acceptance score, and live platform performance.\n\n## Command router\n\nDetect the first command token. Ignore surrounding punctuation, whitespace, and a trailing colon.\n\n| User command | Mode | Required behavior |\n|---|---|---|\n| `选题：` / `topic:` | Structure only | Produce story structure; do not write the full storyboard, generate images, or claim acceptance. |\n| `分镜：` / `storyboard:` | Storyboard | Build the storyboard from an approved or supplied structure; do not silently change the premise. |\n| `验收：` / `acceptance:` | Acceptance | Inspect supplied artifacts and report pass/fail, blockers, and minimum fixes; do not rewrite unless asked. |\n| `自动：` / `auto:` | Full pipeline | Run structure → storyboard → acceptance in order. Stop at a blocking failure and report what must be fixed. Do not generate images or publish unless explicitly requested. |\n| `对比打分：` / `compare score:` | Directory comparison | Require a directory path. The directory must contain at least one of topic/structure, storyboard, or images. Compare all available components across multiple dimensions and score with evidence. |\n\nIf no command is recognizable, explain the five commands briefly and ask the user to prefix the task with one. For `对比打分` without a directory, ask for the directory and do not score from memory. For a directory with no recognized topic/storyboard/image evidence, report insufficient evidence and request the missing path or artifact.\n\n## Non-negotiable mixed-mode rules\n\nThe default mode is:\n\n`节奏模式：混合模式（鼠鼠主行动 + Zayn视觉扩张）`\n\nMixed mode is not a third independent rhythm. It requires both causal systems:\n\n- 鼠鼠 S1-S8: everyday task, emotional anchor, relationship guide, visible anomaly, rule, transgression, physical confrontation, human closure, and aftermath.\n- Zayn Z1-Z8: credible entry, motif shown by image 3, same-source recurrence, rule confirmation, character involvement, scale expansion, event closure, and ending re-read.\n\nHard constraints:\n\n- Default 20 images; maximum 25.\n- Image 3 must show a concrete, directly visible anomaly.\n- The first three images must establish real-world motivation/relationship pressure and the anomaly.\n- Define one anomaly motif as `core form + material/color + motion/growth/mimicry rule`.\n- Use at least three different carriers and three scales; each recurrence must add a new inference.\n- The character must act, not only observe; the real task and relationship must close.\n- The final image must provide physical aftermath and change the meaning of at least two earlier images.\n- Do not use “未完待续” to avoid closure.\n- Do not copy competitor characters, entities, shots, dialogue, or distinctive designs.\n\nRealism guardrails (提炼自 oh-my-folkstoryphoto，适配本项目现有节奏与目录):\n\n- Every new episode must add a short `真实性方案` section to its existing `docs/` topic or storyboard document before image handoff: primary capture device, photographer, why the device is present, 9:16 capture behavior, and stable/restricted/out-of-control image states.\n- Before the full image handoff, run a three-shot visual calibration using the existing P0/四图准入 workflow: ordinary baseline, worst capture condition, and first major anomaly. These are review checkpoints, not extra publish images; approved calibration frames may be reused as the corresponding final frames.\n- Treat viewpoint physics, unplanned recorder/device visibility, capture-profile continuity, and non-cinematic drift as hard acceptance checks. A prompt request alone is not evidence; inspect the returned image when available.\n- Record the calibration result and the approved storyboard/version hash in the episode's existing `docs/` review file. Do not create a parallel state machine or new project directory.\n- Content repair is one round per image. Keep the original candidate and repair decision in the existing episode version directory; a second hard failure is `不通过`/`needs_user`, never silently accepted.\n\n## Mode behavior\n\n### `选题` / `topic`\n\nRead the relevant authority docs, then output only: premise, location, protagonist, real task, emotional anchor, relationship character, anomaly motif, controversy hooks, title candidates with scores, S1-S8, Z1-Z8, motif carriers/scales, proposed 20-image beat map, risks, and a go/no-go structure verdict. Do not output the full per-image prompt set.\n\n### `分镜` / `storyboard`\n\nRequire an approved structure or clearly supplied premise. Output each image’s act, S/Z labels, function, visual content, first-person method, characters/props, caption, caption function, motif carrier, scale, causal link, generation prompt, negative prompt, and continuity risk. Do not add unapproved major lore. Finish with asset-lock and caption checks.\n\n### `验收` / `acceptance`\n\nInspect the supplied text and image artifacts. For images, use visual inspection when available; never mark visual consistency from filenames alone. Classify findings as `必须重出`, `必须改文`, `建议调整`, or `可接受`. Check S/Z completeness, first-three hook, motif recurrence, scale progression, first-person framing, character/prop continuity, captions, closure, originality, and publish readiness. A score is not a pass if a hard blocker remains.\n\n### `自动` / `auto`\n\nRun the three modes sequentially. Preserve approved decisions between stages. If structure fails, do not continue to storyboard. If storyboard fails, do not claim acceptance. If acceptance finds blockers, return the minimum repair list and the final status `有条件通过` or `不通过`. Image generation is a separate action and requires an explicit request.\n\n### `对比打分` / `compare score`\n\nRequire an explicit directory. Inspect every relevant file under it, recognizing Chinese/English filenames and common Markdown/image formats. The directory must contain one or more of:\n\n- topic/structure evidence;\n- storyboard evidence;\n- image evidence.\n\nCompare available entries or versions, never pretend absent components exist. Use these dimensions, scoring each 0-10 with file/image evidence:\n\n1. topic hook and everyday entry;\n2. S1-S8 causal completeness;\n3. Z1-Z8 motif/scale completeness;\n4. first-three retention potential;\n5. narrative causality and information change;\n6. emotional/relationship closure;\n7. ending aftermath and re-read;\n8. motif continuity and originality;\n9. first-person visual realism;\n10. character, prop, and scene consistency;\n11. caption usability and obstruction risk;\n12. production readiness and acceptance risk.\n\nFor each candidate, provide a score table, evidence, weaknesses, confidence, and a ranked recommendation. If only images exist, do not infer the full story causality or captions; mark those dimensions `未提供证据` and exclude them from the normalized total. If only documents exist, do not claim image quality. Use a weighted total only after stating which dimensions were actually scored.\n\n## Output discipline\n\nLead with the verdict. Keep evidence tied to paths and image numbers. Separate facts, inferences, and missing evidence. Do not alter repository files, rewrite story documents, or create images unless the user explicitly asks for that action. When this skill does produce or edit artifacts, finish with:\n\n`【目标】 【改动文件】 【自测结果】 【风险】 【必须验收】 【结论】`\n\n## Language selection\n\nUse `references/zh-CN.md` for Chinese output and `references/en-US.md` for English output. The two references define the same workflow and acceptance gates; keep labels `鼠鼠节奏-S1~S8` and `Zayn节奏-Z1~Z8` alongside translated explanations.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
